    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKGJmZWE1YWRiZWU4ZGI5OTE5NTY5OGYzMGU0NmZiOWQxMzJmZDc3MGY",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local",
        "date": "2026-11-10T19:00:20Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mikekinney@Mikes-MacBook-Pro.local",
        "date": "2026-11-10T19:00:20Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(ui,app): setup alignment composes on the current pose, one flow, readable picks (#738)\n\n- Laying the part on a face or on three points reads the pick through the\n  setup's held alignment and composes the lay onto it\n  (pick::lay_on_plane_in / lay_on_points_in); a re-applied pick is a zero\n  step. Each move stays one AlignPartToSetup undo step.\n- The Part alignment row is one step of the flow: presets and \"Turn by\"\n  turn the part from where it sits now (CommandKind::TurnPart ->\n  AlignPartToSetup::turn_by -> setup_turn::turned_by); \"As modelled\" is\n  the one reset. Tooltips describe the flow.\n- Pick status reads \"1 face selected\", \"2 points selected\", \"1 edge\n  selected\" (ui::pick_words); no internal feature ids on the rows or in\n  pick refusals.\n- The collecting draft's picks paint as filled semi-transparent faces,\n  round filled point discs and bold 4 px edges (ui::align_pick_viz).\n- Split: commands/setup_align.rs's following-stock half moves to\n  commands/align_stock.rs; state.rs's alignment arms move to\n  state_align.rs.\n\nFixes #738\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL",
